SUMMARY:Singin’ in the Rain
DESCRIPTION:Singin’ in the Rain (1952) Directed by Gene Kelly and Stanley Donen. 1hr 43min. Rated G. \n\n\n\nGuest programmed by Drag sensation Poison Waters\, catch Singin’ in the Rain (1952) as part of our film series Pretty\, Witty and Gay—in conversation with the David Hockney exhibition. This magical and celebrated musical comedy focuses on the transition from silent films to “talkies”—exploring the visual landscape of Hollywood through vibrant technicolor\, fantastical rain-soaked choreography\, and colorful costumes. \n\n\n\nWe do not generally provide advisories about subject matter or potentially triggering content in films\, and films exhibited don’t necessarily reflect the views of PAM CUT or the Portland Art Museum. In addition to the synopses\, trailers\, and other links on our website\, further information about content and age-appropriateness for specific films can be found on sites like Common Sense Media\, IMDb\, and DoesTheDogDie.com.
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/singin-in-the-rain/
LOCATION:Portland Art Museum\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
CATEGORIES:PAM CUT @ The Whitsell,Screenings & experiences
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://portlandartmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Singing-in-the-Rain-2-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
