SUMMARY:La Piscine
DESCRIPTION:La Piscine (1969) Directed by Jacques Deray. 2hrs. Rated PG. \n\n\n\nGuest programmed by the fashion in film experts  Looks on Screen\, La Piscine (1969) captures a languid summer in the South of France. Part of our film series Pretty Witty and Gay\, in conversation with the David Hockney exhibit\, the film is set in a luxurious\, vibrant and stylish villa whose pool provides a backdrop for tense drama\, with costume design by André Courrèges. \n\n\n\nWe do not generally provide advisories about subject matter or potentially triggering content in films\, and films exhibited don’t necessarily reflect the views of PAM CUT or the Portland Art Museum. In addition to the synopses\, trailers\, and other links on our website\, further information about content and age-appropriateness for specific films can be found on sites like Common Sense Media\, IMDb\, and DoesTheDogDie.com.
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/la-piscine/
LOCATION:Portland Art Museum\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
CATEGORIES:PAM CUT @ The Whitsell,Screenings & experiences
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://portlandartmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/La-Pacine.jpeg
END:VEVENT
